SUMMARY:Botanical Resin Coaster Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Try something new this summer and join us for an exciting Botanical Resin Coaster Workshop!\nGet creative in this hands-on workshop where you’ll design and make your own set of resin coasters using dried flowers\, foliage\, and decorative elements inspired by nature. In this guided step-by-step\, you’ll learn how to arrange your materials\, pour resin\, and cure your pieces—no experience needed. This beginner-friendly workshop is the perfect way to unwind\, explore your creativity\, and create beautiful\, functional pieces to take home.\n \nAll materials are included\, and each participant will leave with four unique\, nature-inspired coasters.\n \nFriday\, July 17\, 7 to 9 p.m.\nPublic $60\, TBG Members $55 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Epiphanie Belanger\n \nEpiphanie Belanger is the founder of HobbyHub\, a community-driven platform designed to help people try new hobbies in a relaxed environment. What started as a personal curiosity for creative pursuits quickly turned into a mission to make hobbies more accessible\, social\, and fun for beginners.\n \nThrough curated workshops and experiences\, Epiphanie brings people together to explore hands-on creative skills in a welcoming\, low-pressure environment. Epiphanie is passionate about helping people rediscover play\, slow down\, and connect (both with their creativity and with others) one hobby at a time.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/botanical-resin-coaster-workshop/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/657d2067ca00ef4e95d0dc6bc3e8bcf2.jpg
END:VEVENT
