UID:10001981-1784881800-1784887200@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Adornment from the Earth: Flower Garland-Making with Grounding & Movement
DESCRIPTION:Connect with nature in this somatic wellness experience at Toronto Botanical Garden!\nThis 90-minute workshop offers creative ritual\, environmental care\, and embodied expression\, using freshly cut\, natural florals and leaves as a bridge between self and nature. By blending the beauty and biodiversity of Toronto Botanical Garden with body-based awareness\, this program embodies the Garden’s vision of bridging the gap between wellness and nature.\n \nFriday\, July 24\, 8:30 to 10 a.m.\nPublic $95\, TBG Members $80 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Anika Rasheed\nAnika Rasheed (she/her) is a trauma-informed somatic practitioner\, sound healer\, and wellness facilitator. She helps individuals regulate their nervous system using trauma-informed\, body-based healing like somatic movement\, breathwork\, and mindfulness/meditation.\n \nWith a background in psychology\, public service\, and holistic wellness\, she bridges science and embodied wisdom to offer practical tools for navigating stress\, trauma\, and emotional overwhelm to strengthen the mind-body connection.\n \nShe has facilitated sessions for community organizations\, corporate workplaces\, universities\, schools\, retirement homes\, and women’s circles\, empowering participants to connect to their mind and body for ease and calm.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n\n\nAdditional Program Information\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/adornment-from-the-earth-flower-garland-making-with-grounding-movement/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
