SUMMARY:Free Edwards Summer Music Series: Medusa Quartet
DESCRIPTION:Medusa Quartet is a genre-defying chamber-folk ensemble reimagining the string quartet through global traditions\, original compositions\, and storytelling. Their distinctive sound features rare and historically revived instruments\, including the Polish suka and fidel\, and the Swedish nyckelharpa\, creating a sonic palette unlike any other in Canada and beyond. \n\n\n\nBlending Middle Eastern\, Scandinavian\, Celtic\, Appalachian\, classical\, and Eastern European influences\, the band connects audiences across cultures and identities. Their 2024 Canadian Folk Music Award–nominated debut EP earned national and international attention through festival appearances across Canada\, the US\, and the UK\, along with CBC\, CKUA\, and Polish National Radio features. \n\n\n\nThursday\, July 30 at 7 p.m.\n\n\n\nFree outdoor concert \n\n\n\nSee the rest of the Edwards Summer Music Series lineup here. \n\n\n\nThis concert is part of the Edwards Summer Music Series\, which showcases diverse\, contemporary talent set within the natural beauty of the garden. Enjoy eight FREE outdoor concerts in the Garden on Thursday nights at 7 p.m. in July and August. General seating is available on a first-come basis. Guests can also bring their own chairs. Concerts are held rain or shine. \n\n\n\nThe Edwards Summer Music Series is generously supported by the Edwards Charitable Foundation and the presenting Sponsor Foresters Financial.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/free-edwards-summer-music-series-medusa-quartet/
LOCATION:ON
CATEGORIES:Edwards Summer Music Series
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/MEDUSA.jpg
END:VEVENT
