SUMMARY:Morning Yoga in the Garden
DESCRIPTION:Start your day with a nature hike through the gardens on your way to an outdoor yoga class at Toronto Botanical Garden.\nThis all-levels yoga class combines mindful movement\, breath awareness\, and relaxation techniques to support strength\, mobility\, balance\, and overall well-being.\n \nParticipants will be guided through accessible yoga postures and movement practices designed to help release tension\, improve flexibility\, and cultivate a sense of calm and connection. The natural beauty of the Garden provides the perfect setting to slow down\, recharge\, and enjoy a mindful start to the day.\n \nEnjoy some mint tea from the Garden before heading back to The George and Kathy Dembroski Centre for Horticulture to complete your visit. Feel free to bring a mug for tea!\n \nNo prior yoga experience is required. Modifications and options will be offered to accommodate a range of abilities and experience levels.\n \nPlease bring your own yoga mat and any props that help you feel comfortable and supported in your practice.\n \nPlease meet at the TBG main entrance\, just outside the George and Kathy Dembroski Centre for Horticulture promptly at 8:15 a.m. Participants will be led on a short walk to the yoga location.\n \nThis is an outdoor yoga class. In the case of dangerous or severe weather\, the program will be moved indoors. Please note\, the walk up to the grounds includes a short walk uphill with some steps and uneven slopes. If you have any accessibility concerns\, please reach out to programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\n \nFriday\, August 7\, 8:15 to 10 a.m.\nPublic $20\, TBG Members $15 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Laura Bianchi\nLaura is a certified yoga therapist and yoga teacher based in Toronto. She offers group yoga classes and individualized yoga therapy sessions that support physical\, emotional\, and nervous system wellbeing through safe\, adaptive\, and thoughtfully guided practices.\n \nLaura has experience working with diverse populations and specializes in creating accessible\, inclusive classes that help participants improve mobility\, reduce stress\, build resilience\, and cultivate a deeper connection with their bodies. Her teaching style is warm\, supportive\, and focused on meeting each person where they are\, making yoga approachable and beneficial for people of all ages and experience levels.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/morning-yoga-in-the-garden/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Wellness
